Feature: bira init

  Scenario: Init creates a project in the current directory
    When I run "bira init --name my-project"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Initialized project"
    And output contains "my-project"
    And file ".bira" exists

  Scenario: Init uses directory name when --name is omitted
    When I run "bira init"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Initialized project"
    And output contains "smoko-work"

  Scenario: Init with --name flag sets the project name
    When I run "bira init --name custom-name"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "custom-name"

  Scenario: Init --json returns structured project output
    When I run "bira init --name json-proj --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "\"name\": \"json-proj\""
    And output contains "\"id\":"

  Scenario: Init fails when already initialized
    When I run "sh -c 'bira init --name first && bira init --name second'"
    Then exit code is not 0
